rolls_royce.premium_reason:
In S1 there is no premium: hold equals the best plan (+14.95). Across scenarios we declare a doctrine premium of about $0.46B in expectation: committing to the Joint Venture would add +2.28 only if P&W commits this round (S4: +17.23 against +14.95), at P(S4) about 0.20. Rolls-Royce would accept this for four reasons:
- it does not commit to a Joint Venture with P&W before the partner's commitment is public, which is our hard rule and our round-1 public statement;
- the IAE exit and P&W's IAE LLC show partners falling out of alignment, and P&W keeps 59-61% of its narrowbody collaborations [R-0318, R-1892, R-1893];
- a standing commitment would let P&W pick the round in which the Joint Venture forms;
- 'we don't commit that easily' [RX-0124].
